Here is a simple example of how you can create a page with an input box that stores whatever text the user types into it. This example uses HTML and JavaScript.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Input Box Example</title>
</head>
<body>
  <input type="text" id="userInput" placeholder="Type something here...">

  <script>
    // This script will store whatever text the user types into the input box
    var userInput = document.getElementById('userInput');
    userInput.addEventListener('input', function() {
      var text = userInput.value;
      console.log(text);
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

